+msgctxt "#33146"
+msgid "Which internal disks this system sees while the setting above shows them. One that is not ticked is kept away from the kernel from the next start: before anything else runs, the system lets go of it, and from then on the kernel attaches no other internal disk and runs with its lockdown, as in the normal start. So neither Kodi, nor its add-ons, nor a program that runs here with full rights can reach it. Only NVMe and SATA disks can be kept away, and never the one this system is on. Disks are told apart by their model and serial number, not by names such as sda, which can change from one start to the next. A choice holds from the next start."
